hadiths[8]{hadithnumber,text}:
"937","970 - Abu Said al-Ashajj narrated to us, he said: Uqba - meaning Ibn Khalid - narrated to me, from Ibn Abi Aruba, from Qatada, from Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sacrificed two horned black-and-white rams."
"938","971 - Harun ibn Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Qasim, from his father, from Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to sacrifice cows on behalf of his wives."
"939","972 - al-Hasan ibn Muhammad al-Zafarani narrated to us, he said: Shababa narrated to us, he said: Zuhayr narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not slaughter except a musinna, unless it is difficult for you, then slaughter a jadhaa of sheep."
"940","973 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Abd al-Hakam informed us that Ibn Wahb informed them, he said: Amr ibn al-Harith informed me, that Bukayr ibn Abdullah ibn al-Ashajj narrated to him, that Muadh ibn Abdullah ibn Khubayb al-Juhani narrated to him, from Uqba ibn Amir al-Juhani, who said: We sacrificed with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a jadha of sheep."
"941","974 - Ali ibn Khashram narrated to us, he said: Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash informed me. And Muhammad ibn Hisham narrated to us, he said: Abu Bakr narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Shurayh ibn al-Numan al-Hamdani, that Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, said - and Ibn Hisham said, from Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade us sacrificing a muqabala, a mudabara, a sharqa, a kharqa, or a jadaa."
"942","975 - Ali ibn Khashram narrated to us, he said: Isa informed me, from Shuba, from Sulayman ibn Abd al-Rahman - freedman of Banu Asad - who said: I heard Ubayd ibn Fayruz - a man of Banu Shayban - say: I asked al-Bara ibn Azib, may Allah be pleased with them both: What did the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) dislike among sacrifices, or what did he forbid? He said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Four do not suffice - and my hand is shorter than his: the one-eyed whose blindness is clear, the lame whose lameness is clear, the sick whose sickness is clear, and the broken-boned that has no marrow. I said: I dislike any defect in the tooth, or in the horn, or any defect in the ear? He said: Whatever you dislike, leave it, but do not forbid it to anyone."
"943","976 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, he said: Dawud ibn Ali informed me, from al-Shabi, from al-Bara ibn Azib, may Allah be pleased with them both, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let none slaughter before praying. My maternal uncle Abu Burda ibn Niyar stood to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, this is a day in which meat is abundant, and I slaughtered my sacrifice so my family and neighbors may eat from it, and I have a young goat better than two meat sheep; shall I slaughter it? He said: Yes, but no jadhaa will suffice for anyone after you, and it is the better of your two sacrifices."
"944","977 - Ali ibn Khashram narrated to us, he said: Isa informed me, from Shuba, from Qatada, who said: I heard Anas ibn Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, say - so I said: Did you hear it? He said: Yes - The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to sacrifice two black-and-white horned rams, pronouncing the name and the takbir; I saw them both as he slaughtered them with his hand, placing his foot upon their sides."
